# Skills permitted to exceed their size cap, per ADR 005.
#
# This file is a backlog, not a settings file. Every line is a debt, and adding
# one shows up in a diff so the exception is argued rather than assumed. The
# caps and the tiers live in scripts/token-budget.sh.
#
# Each line is `<skill> <bytes>`. The bytes are the size that
# `make token-report` measures, plus a headroom of 20 bytes. Add a line only
# for a skill the report shows over its cap. The bytes are a ratchet:
# `make lint` fails when a listed skill over its cap grows past them. A PR
# that shrinks a skill sets its number to the new size plus 20. A PR that must
# grow one raises the number in its diff and says why. Delete the line when
# the skill is back under its cap.
#
# The measured size includes the version: line that CI stamps after each
# merge, and the length of the stamp changes: a micro suffix such as .1 or .12
# adds 2 or 3 bytes. The headroom absorbs that change and a small growth of
# the content. When `make lint` fails on several listed skills whose content
# did not change, the headroom is used up. To fix it, run `make token-report`,
# and in one PR set each listed skill to its measured size plus 20.

